## Healthy changes

If you are overweight, losing even **5% of your body weight** can make periods more regular, improve symptoms and lower the risk of diabetes. Being active helps your body use insulin better, whatever your weight.

## Irregular periods

- the **combined contraceptive pill** can make periods regular and protect the lining of the womb
- if you do not use the pill, you may be offered a **progestogen** medicine to bring on a period every few months, or a **hormonal coil**

## Extra hair and acne

- the **combined pill** can reduce hair growth and acne
- **eflornithine cream** can slow facial hair growth
- treatments for [acne](/conditions/skin/acne/)
- hair removal, such as laser treatment, is usually not available on the NHS

## Metformin

**Metformin**, a diabetes medicine, is sometimes used to help with insulin resistance, periods and weight, though it is not licensed for PCOS.

## Fertility

If you are trying to get pregnant, you may be offered:

- **letrozole** or **clomifene**, medicines that help you release an egg
- **metformin**, alone or with these medicines
- a small operation called **ovarian drilling**
- **IVF**, if other treatments do not work
